Jahshaka patch 0075 (claimed 0074 in the lane; renumbered at merge — 0074 is PHOTON-M1's composite) — a LOD switch has a hysteresis band.

SOURCE patch. EVERY TREE MUST RE-RUN `irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` after
pulling this. It touches `OgreMain/include/OgreLodStrategy.h`,
`OgreMain/include/OgreLodStrategyPrivate.inl` and
`OgreMain/src/OgreLodStrategy.cpp`, which NO other patch in this stack touches,
so there is no overlap to reset for.

WHY A PATCH AND NOT A WORKAROUND (owner rule, 2026-09-15, ledger §325).
`LodStrategy::lodSet` picks a level with ONE `std::lower_bound` against the
mesh's value array and writes `MovableObject::mCurrentMeshLod`
(OgreLodStrategyPrivate.inl:31-40). The comparison is a step in both
directions, so an object whose LOD value sits ON a threshold changes level
EVERY FRAME the value dithers — a camera breathing at a switch distance, a
dolly crawling across one, a hand-held pose in a headset. Stage 1 of ATOM ships
with no defence against it and no suite measured it (the render audit's A7).

The band cannot be written outside the pin:

  * `mCurrentMeshLod` and `mLodMesh` are PROTECTED on `MovableObject`
    (OgreMovableObject.h:122-123) and the friendship it grants is to
    `LodStrategy::lodSet` and `LodStrategy::lodUpdateImpl` BY NAME
    (OgreMovableObject.h:354-356) — friendship to a base class's virtual
    member does not extend to a derived class's override, so a strategy of our
    own (which is how the rest of ATOM-3's view rule is written, with no patch
    at all) can compute a VALUE but can never see or hold the level;
  * a hysteresis expressed in the value alone needs the direction of travel,
    i.e. per-object state, and `ObjectData` has no slot for it;
  * `getCurrentMeshLod()` is public, but without the mesh's thresholds — which
    are the protected `mLodMesh` — knowing the current level says nothing about
    how far the value is from the switch.

So the band belongs where the comparison is, and it is eleven lines there.

WHAT IT DOES. `LodStrategy::setHysteresis( fraction )` is process-wide and
defaults to 0, which is upstream's behaviour to the bit: with no band the
function is the same `lower_bound` it always was. With a band `h`, a switch to
a COARSER level requires the value to pass the crossed threshold by
`h * |threshold|` and a switch back to a FINER one requires it to fall below by
the same, so the level only moves when the picture would genuinely change and a
value that is genuinely past the band moves on the frame it gets there. The
band is RELATIVE, so it means the same thing in every strategy's units
(distances, pixel counts, or Jahshaka's world-space errors), and it can only
ever hold the CURRENT level — a multi-level jump still jumps all the way, and
nothing can be held for more than the band's width of travel.

MEASURED (ATOM-3, spikes/atom-3/FINDINGS.md §4), in FRAMES and not in seconds:
one chained mesh alone in the scene, the camera oscillating sinusoidally about
its level-1 switch distance (3.836 m), 600 frames, a level change counted every
frame the drawn triangle count moves. The oscillation crosses the threshold 71
times in those 600 frames.

  amplitude   band 0 (upstream)   band 0.10 (ours)
  +-2 %       71 pops, 2 levels   0 pops, 1 level
  +-20 %      71 pops, 2 levels   71 pops, 2 levels

So the band removes exactly the pops that are noise — every crossing of a
motion too small to change the picture — and keeps every crossing of a motion
that is real. Jahshaka sets 0.10 once, in `installJahLodStrategy`
(irisgl/engine/src/OgreMesh.cpp), behind the run-wide `JAHSHAKA_NO_LOD_HYSTERESIS`
latch that took the "band 0" column above. One consequence to know: with a band
the switch distance depends on the direction of approach, by the width of the
band — the same bisection reads 3.836 m with it off and 4.047 m with it on.

Verified: `git apply --check` against the pristine pin, and
`git apply --reverse --check` after applying.
diff --git a/OgreMain/include/OgreLodStrategy.h b/OgreMain/include/OgreLodStrategy.h
index 4230220bf..650975c49 100644
--- a/OgreMain/include/OgreLodStrategy.h
+++ b/OgreMain/include/OgreLodStrategy.h
@@ -108,6 +108,28 @@ namespace Ogre
 
         /** Get the name of this strategy. */
         const String &getName() const { return mName; }
+
+        /** JAHSHAKA (ogre-patch 0075): the LOD SWITCH HYSTERESIS BAND, as a
+            fraction of the threshold being crossed. 0 (the default) is this
+            engine's historical behaviour exactly: `lodSet` flips at the exact
+            threshold in both directions, so an object sitting on one pops
+            between two levels every frame the camera jitters.
+
+            With a band `h`, a switch to a COARSER level needs the value to pass
+            the threshold by `h * |threshold|`, and a switch back to a FINER one
+            needs it to fall below by the same amount. The band is relative, so
+            it is meaningful whatever a strategy's units are, and it is bounded:
+            a value genuinely past the band switches on the frame it gets there,
+            and a jump of several levels is still one step.
+
+            Process-wide and written once at startup; read by the worker threads
+            that run `lodUpdateImpl`. */
+        static void setHysteresis( Real fraction ) { msHysteresis = fraction > 0 ? fraction : 0; }
+        static Real getHysteresis() { return msHysteresis; }
+
+    protected:
+        /// @see setHysteresis. Defined in OgreLodStrategy.cpp.
+        static Real msHysteresis;
     };
     /** @} */
     /** @} */
diff --git a/OgreMain/include/OgreLodStrategyPrivate.inl b/OgreMain/include/OgreLodStrategyPrivate.inl
index ea7243f81..87de02758 100644
--- a/OgreMain/include/OgreLodStrategyPrivate.inl
+++ b/OgreMain/include/OgreLodStrategyPrivate.inl
@@ -39,8 +39,31 @@ namespace Ogre
             {
                 FastArray<Real>::const_iterator it =
                     std::lower_bound( owner->mLodMesh->begin(), owner->mLodMesh->end(), lodValues[j] );
-                owner->mCurrentMeshLod =
-                    static_cast<uint8>( std::max<ptrdiff_t>( it - owner->mLodMesh->begin() - 1, 0 ) );
+                ptrdiff_t newLod = std::max<ptrdiff_t>( it - owner->mLodMesh->begin() - 1, 0 );
+
+                // JAHSHAKA (ogre-patch 0075): THE HYSTERESIS BAND. Without it
+                // this comparison is a step in both directions, so an object
+                // parked on a threshold — a camera breathing at a switch
+                // distance, a dolly crawling past one — changes level every
+                // frame. The band is measured on the threshold actually being
+                // crossed, which is the only one that matters here, and it can
+                // only ever hold the CURRENT level: a value past the band moves,
+                // and a several-level jump moves all the way.
+                const ptrdiff_t curLod = static_cast<ptrdiff_t>( owner->mCurrentMeshLod );
+                if( msHysteresis > 0 && newLod != curLod &&
+                    curLod < static_cast<ptrdiff_t>( owner->mLodMesh->size() ) )
+                {
+                    const Real threshold = newLod > curLod ? ( *owner->mLodMesh )[size_t( curLod + 1 )]
+                                                           : ( *owner->mLodMesh )[size_t( curLod )];
+                    const Real band = Math::Abs( threshold ) * msHysteresis;
+                    if( newLod > curLod ? ( lodValues[j] < threshold + band )
+                                        : ( lodValues[j] > threshold - band ) )
+                    {
+                        newLod = curLod;
+                    }
+                }
+
+                owner->mCurrentMeshLod = static_cast<uint8>( newLod );
             }
 
             RenderableArray::iterator itor = owner->mRenderables.begin();
